NAME
    qml-rules - check that QML files hold layout only, as the Qt front end requires

SYNOPSIS
    qml-rules [--fixture] <path>...

DESCRIPTION
    The development tool of the emusen.dev module for the Qt front end's
    rule (EmuSen_Qt.md §1.3): a QML file arranges, binds and calls into
    models; every decision is Rust's. Each <path> is a .qml file or a
    directory searched for .qml files (a 'target' folder is skipped).
    Findings print one a line:

        file:line rule words

    and the last line is 'ok' or 'N findings'. The rules, with the
    checker's name for each:

        function     a function, other than a Connections handler of the
                     form 'function onX(...) { one.call() }'
        callLater    Qt.callLater
        literal      an array or object literal built in QML
        words        a string the player would read, outside the bindings
                     that take a name (objectName, font.family, source,
                     fragmentShader, vertexShader, property, properties,
                     sequence, Accessible.role, placeholderText) and colour
                     literals ('#rrggbb', 'transparent')
        onCompleted  Component.onCompleted doing more than taking the
                     focus
        rows         a ListModel with ListElement rows
        import       a module outside QtQuick, QtQuick.Controls,
                     QtQuick.Templates, QtQuick.Layouts, QtQuick.Shapes,
                     QtQml (never QtQml.Models) and EmuSen.*; or the kit
                     imported unqualified, since every file writes
                     'import EmuSen.Kit as Kit' so that Qt's Frame and
                     the kit's never shadow each other

    --fixture reads the paths as fixtures (test scenes, the gallery):
    their words, rows and literals stand in for the models a screen
    would have, so the words, rows and literal rules are off and the
    others hold.

EXIT STATUS
    0 for no finding, 1 for one or more, 2 when it could not run (a path
    missing, an option unknown).

EXAMPLES
    qml-rules Frontend/kit-qt
    qml-rules --fixture Frontend/qt-test/qml Frontend/kit-gallery/qml
    qml-rules themes/night/Main.qml

SEE ALSO
    dupes(1), hwcount(1); EmuSen_Qt.md §1.3 and §8.4; EmuSen_Kit.md §7.9.
